sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: In any triangle, if one of the sides is produced, then the exterior angle equals the sum of the two interior and opposite angles, and the sum of the three interior angles of the triangle equals two right angles.
----
proof:

Let {ABC} be a triangle, and let one side of it {BC} be produced to {D}.

I say that the exterior angle {ACD} equals the sum of the two interior and opposite angles {CAB} and {ABC|CBA}, and the sum of the three interior angles of the triangle {ABC|CBA}, {BCA}, and {CAB} equals two right angles.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="240" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="I.32 diagram" src="propI32.gif"/></noscript>
